# Adding a resource appends to exactly two shared files: one property on the root client interface
# and the [JsonSerializable] entries for its DTOs. When resources are built in parallel branches those
# appends always land in the same region, and the correct resolution is always "keep both". The union
# driver does that automatically. It is safe here precisely because the edits are append-only by
# convention (see CLAUDE.md) - do not extend it to files where two branches can rewrite the same line.
src/GitLab.Client/Abstractions/IGitLabClient.cs merge=union
src/GitLab.Client/Infrastructure/Serialization/GitLabJsonContext.cs merge=union
